WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:05.200
It's safe to say that Hermione Granger and&nbsp;
Ron Weasley have always been the endgame&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:10.000
in the "Harry Potter" universe. Both of these&nbsp;
Gryffindors are beloved fantasy characters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:14.160
and they’ve always been favorably shipped&nbsp;
together. However, one particular scene&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:19.520
revolving around the two characters' relationship&nbsp;
wasn't quite as romantic. In "Harry Potter and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:24.960
the Chamber of Secrets," Emma Watson was quite&nbsp;
nervous to film a particular scene as Hermione…&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:30.080
and apparently angry with the movie's director&nbsp;
Chris Columbus for making her do it anyway.

00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:33.360
There's a particular scene at the&nbsp;
end of the film in which Hermione&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:37.600
has to run into the Great Hall and hug&nbsp;
both Harry and Ron. However, the shy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:42.640
then-11-year-old Watson was too embarrassed to hug&nbsp;
both of the boys in front of the cast and crew.

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:47.040
Columbus tried to work around things&nbsp;
by making Watson hug Daniel Radcliffe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:52.480
and shake Rupert Grint's hand instead. Watson was&nbsp;
even embarrassed to hug Radcliffe for too long,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.480 --> 00:00:56.560
so their hug had to be frozen for a&nbsp;
few seconds longer than it actually was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.560 --> 00:01:01.680
for it to appear more realistic on-screen. The&nbsp;
actress has since opened up on Instagram about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:05.760
how nerve-wracking it was to film that&nbsp;
scene with everybody on set watching.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:10.280
Watson even said that her arms&nbsp;
barely touched around his neck.

00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:14.240
“You laugh, but this is actually&nbsp;
quite traumatic for me.”

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:17.840
The result of the scene actually ended&nbsp;
up working perfectly for the storyline&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:21.760
of Ron and Hermione. The fans of the&nbsp;
"Harry Potter" books and films know&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:25.840
of the underlying feelings that both&nbsp;
characters have for each other. Hermione&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:31.280
even ends up marrying the endearing redhead at the&nbsp;
conclusion of the series. If you're a true fan,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:34.800
you're up to speed on everything that&nbsp;
happens throughout their relationship.

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:38.400
Adapting books into movies can be&nbsp;
extremely challenging, and many&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:43.120
details are often altered in the process.&nbsp;
Despite some of the major changes that had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:47.120
to be made to fit within the restrictions&nbsp;
of filming the second "Harry Potter" movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:50.640
"Harry Potter and the Chamber of&nbsp;
Secrets" still holds up today.

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:55.520
Watson, Grint, and Radcliffe definitely grew&nbsp;
closer over the years as the movie franchise&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.520 --> 00:02:00.720
went on. However, it seems like the actress's&nbsp;
attitude towards filming more intimate scenes with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:06.640
her co-stars never changed. In "Harry Potter and&nbsp;
the Deathly Hallows: Part 1," one of the Horcruxes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:12.480
shows Ron a vision of one of his biggest fears. It&nbsp;
just so happens to be Hermione and Harry kissing.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:17.680
The vision is strange and intense, and Watson and&nbsp;
Radcliffe had to make it look really passionate.

00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:21.120
Speaking with “The Seattle Times,”&nbsp;
Watson said that the experience&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:25.360
filming the kiss with Radcliffe was,&nbsp;
quote, "bloody awkward,” explaining,

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:27.760
“Dan and I are like brother and sister."

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:31.200
But, unlike her younger self,&nbsp;
she put her all into the scene,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:35.680
following director David Yates's directions&nbsp;
with the hope that it might help them finish&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:39.680
filming more quickly. As the scene is&nbsp;
supposed to be a vision seen by Ron,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:45.040
Grint was originally on set to watch them kiss&nbsp;
and give accurate reactions. But apparently,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:50.000
Grint couldn't control his emotions at seeing&nbsp;
his two best friends making out. Grint Shared,

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:54.000
"Emma sent me out because I kept&nbsp;
laughing. It just looked really strange."

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:58.400
This scene is definitely more hands-on&nbsp;
than the "Chamber of Secrets" hug,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:02.240
and Watson held it all together to get&nbsp;
the filming done. It wasn't even the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.240 --> 00:03:06.400
only kissing scene she had to do for the&nbsp;
franchise. Ron and Hermione finally make&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:11.040
their romance official with a kiss in "Harry&nbsp;
Potter and the Deathly Hallows: Part 2."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:15.920
Being as close to Grint as she is with&nbsp;
Radcliffe, Watson told “Movies Ireland,”

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:20.080
"Believe me, we both wanted it to be&nbsp;
over equally as much as the other.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:23.360
It's honestly like kissing&nbsp;
my brother. It was weird."

00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:27.440
Despite how they felt in real life, the&nbsp;
kiss is a very important moment for Ron&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:30.320
and Hermione's relationship on-screen. Thankfully,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.320 --> 00:03:34.640
the two actors successfully overcame the&nbsp;
awkwardness to make it look realistic.

